cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "lgpsf: Laguerre-Gaussian point-spread-function operator approximation"
abstract: >-
  A header-only C++17 library (with Python bindings) that compresses a large,
  dense, matrix-free operator into a sparse one from its action on random
  vectors. Each row is fitted as a Laguerre-Gaussian expansion on its own
  ellipsoid by variable projection, plus a discrete spike correction, and the
  result is deployable as a sparse matrix, a matvec, or a continuum kernel. The
  probe count does not grow under mesh refinement. Motivated by Gauss-Newton
  Hessians in PDE-constrained inverse problems, where applying the operator is
  expensive and its entries are not available.
type: software
authors:
